[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"pdf-compression-guide\",\n    \"title\": \"The Ultimate Guide to PDF Compression: Shrink Files Like a Pro\",\n    \"description\": \"Learn how to reduce PDF file size without losing quality. Complete DPI benchmarks, Flate vs JPEG compression, and step-by-step optimization rules.\",\n    \"keywords\": [\"pdf compression\", \"reduce pdf size\", \"compress pdf\", \"pdf optimization\"],\n    \"category\": \"pdf\",\n    \"readTime\": \"8 min read\",\n    \"sections\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Introduction to Document Optimization\",\n        \"content\": \"Large PDF files are a persistent challenge in digital workflows. Whether you are submitting a job application on a government portal with strict file size limits (often under 2MB), emailing detailed client reports, or optimizing server storage costs, knowing how to shrink PDF documents efficiently is an essential technical skill. A poorly optimized PDF can lead to slow downloads, failed email attachments, and bloated archiving costs. Fortunately, modern compression algorithms allow us to significantly reduce document footprints while maintaining clean, legible typography and high-definition visual assets.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"How PDF Compression Works Under the Hood\",\n        \"content\": \"A PDF (Portable Document Format) is not a flat canvas; it is a complex object graph containing vector shapes, text coordinates, embedded fonts, metadata schemas, and raster images. The compiler reduces a PDF's size using several core methods: First, Image Downsampling lowers the DPI (dots per inch) of embedded photos. Second, Lossless Flate compression is applied to text streams and vector tables, while lossy JPEG compression is used on photographs to discard invisible color frequencies. Third, Font Subsetting strips unused characters from embedded font containers. Finally, Metadata Pruning deletes XML records and layout histories that add unnecessary bulk to the file.\"\n      }